    "background_story": "Samuel was a grizzled fisherman who spent his life on the open waters. He had heard tales of the elusive 'Ravehook', a mythical fish said to appear only under the light of a full moon. Determined to catch the beast, Samuel spent years studying the tides and patterns of the sea. One fateful night, as the moon hung low in the sky, Samuel cast his line into the depths. The wait was agonizing, but finally, his hook was tugged by an unseen force. With a mighty heave, Samuel reeled in the Ravehook, its scales shimmering in the moonlight. The catch made him a legend among fishermen, but Samuel knew the true magic lay not in the fish itself, but in the mystery of the sea and the thrill of the hunt.",
